I missed the thread in which this was decided (got a link?), but I
have serious issues with the reasoning.  Random is -good-, for it
gives individual games more character.  "That was the game in which I
found a scroll of genocide on level 3" is more memorable than "That
was the game I found a balanced selection of items relevant to my
power level."  If a player wins because he was extremely lucky that
one game, that's not a bad thing.  I'd say that overall, the player
should have to rely more on randomly-generated stuff, and less on
things he can get every time by making or Castle-wishing for them, or
finding them guaranteed.


